From 6c599edcf6591a533d87cd0b20ce1f0cbc6a4537 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:43:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 19/97] graphics: per-phase GPU command thread census; drop
 per-write/per-draw lookup overhead

Diagnostics (env-gated by WWE13_RATE_CENSUS, no-op otherwise): exclusive
wall time and call counts per command-processor phase (WAIT_REG_MEM, draw,
copy, swap, submit) and the top WAIT_REG_MEM poll targets, logged once per
second as [rate-census-cp].

Performance (no behaviour change): CommandProcessor::WriteRegister checked
every register write against GetRegisterInfo (a large switch of guarded
statics) only to decide on a debug log line; it now uses a table built once
from register_table.inc. Readback resolve/memexport cvar decisions were
re-derived with string/map work per draw and per copy; they are now cached
when a guest frame opens. Measured on the WWE 13 entrance: GPU command thread
-2.2 ms per frame (register-write path 6.95 -> 4.25 ms/frame).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
